    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d89">

                <pb facs="0095" n="89" xml:id="pg89"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.0146/705: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-09-29T18:00:00-05:00">September 29, 1939—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>378. Your 869, September 29, 11 a.m. Department approves statement made by you to
                    the Mayor of the Japanese-sponsored Chinese Municipal regime as reported in your
                    telegram under reference.</p>
                <p>Sent to Shanghai. Repeated to Chungking and Peiping. Shanghai please air mail to
                    Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
